<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL -- Agouron surges on earnings.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL -- Agouron surges on earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Agouron Pharmaceuticals Inc surged  in pre-opening trading after the company said it earned $0.17 a share  before a special charge, compared to a loss of $0.17 a share last  year.</p>
<p>Shares were up to to 102-1/2, traders said, from a closing Nasdaq  price of 95-3/4.</p>
<p>Augouron also set a two-for-one stock split. The company's protease  inhibitor, Viracept, is used in a three-drug cocktail to fight HIV.</p>
</text>
